## interests
### assembly coding
Working close to the hardware, optimizing, understanding systems.
=> https://www.youtube.com/@enthusi YouTube channel

### reverse engineering
Understanding how games and systems really work.
=> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=scKGmxWP1mE A talk I gave on Point and click adventure engines

### low-level game development
Retro systems, constraints, creative engineering.
C64, Atari 2600, Lynx, PC-98, PC-FX, Alice Matra, Virtual Boy, SNES, Jupiter Ace
=> https://priorartgames.eu PriorArt, our indie game dev group

=> playdate/index.gmi Playdate voxel engine
=> alice/index.gmi Alice Matra Assembloids
=> neogeo/index.gmi Game Development for the NeoGeo CD

### astronomy
Research, instrumentation, and the bigger picture.
My profession and passion ♥

### analog photography
Pinhole cameras, cyanotype, light without shortcuts.

### linux
Simple tools, direct control, no unnecessary layers.

### riscV
Clean architectures, transparent design. Wonderful Assembly opcode space.

### cycling
Single speed. Minimal. Direct.

### other interests
* GO (the board game) - but I soon realised that it's an never ending journey that I better do not get TOO deep into if I ever want to get other things done.
* Japan language - but I soon realised ... still on it though. It is amazing and prevents brain rot (such goes my theory at least).

